From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:21:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 092/190] segacd: the timeshare is opt-in -- Right held, never
 by default

Engaging the firmware automatically put its first visit inside
EmuTOS's boot, and that is where it took the machine: a console
stopped at the version banner with a frozen HUD, unable to reach even
the diagnostic. The mechanism is plain -- a visit masks the gate array
to levels 4 and 5 and restores it on the way out, so a firmware call
that does not return leaves levels 2 and 3 off forever, EmuTOS's 200 Hz
clock never ticks again, and the banner waits for a tick that is never
coming. My loops have timeouts; the BIOS's own calls do not.

Default is the driver that at least boots. Hold Right to hand D: to
the firmware.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 54cf3d5..7e8d8a1 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -145,6 +145,7 @@ static UBYTE cdd_count, cdd_good;
 static UBYTE cdd_tick;
 static UBYTE cdd_cmd_on;        /* holding A at power-on turns these off */
 UBYTE segacd_diag;              /* holding Down runs the D: diagnostic */
+static UBYTE cd_ts_want;        /* Right held: let the firmware drive D: */
 static UBYTE cd_selftest;       /* holding Up runs the boot sector test */
 UWORD segacd_bootflags;         /* the raw button word the servant sent.
                                  * Printed by the diagnostic, because a
@@ -451,6 +452,7 @@ void segacd_cdd_init(void)
         segacd_diag = (UBYTE)((f & 4) ? 1 : 0);
         cd_lead = (f & 8) ? 2UL : 20UL;
         cd_selftest = (UBYTE)((f & 16) ? 1 : 0);
+        cd_ts_want = (UBYTE)((f & 32) ? 1 : 0);
         segacd_bootflags = (UWORD)(f & 0xFF);
     }
 
@@ -2222,7 +2224,7 @@ static BOOL cd_read_block(ULONG block, UBYTE *buf)
      * moment -- one drive, one master. */
     if (!cd_ts_decided) {
         cd_ts_decided = 1;
-        if (segacd_bios_available()) {
+        if (cd_ts_want && segacd_bios_available()) {
             cd_ts = 1;
             cdd_cmd_on = 0;     /* our VBL stops talking to the drive */
         }
